# Perennation: "Return target permanent card from your graveyard to the battlefield with a hexproof counter and an indestructible counter on it." Bot2's
# Lightning Bolt kills Bot1's Ornithopter on turn 2; on turn 3 Perennation (six mana: five Moxen and an Island) returns it with both counters, and it
# comes back as the same 0/2 it was. The Bolt is an instant and the only other card in either graveyard, so the Ornithopter is the one legal target.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Ornithopter
Island
Perennation
Mox Ruby
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Island x30

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Ornithopter)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Perennation.Cast(Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.Hexproof = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.Indestructible = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Toughness = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = false
Bot1.Graveyard = Perennation
Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
